   "answer": "The March 2026 payment-processing delays were traced to two separate system changes.\n\n* **Deposit-processing delay (INC-2041, 12 Mar 2026)** - caused by\n  * **CHG-1042** - reduced the PayFlex connection-pool max size in *payment-gateway* from 200 to 50 (deployed 2026-03-09) [\u200bS1\u200b].\n  * **CHG-1051** - released fraud-scoring model v3.2 (deployed 2026-03-12 09:15 UTC) [\u200bS1\u200b].\n  * Affected services were *payment-gateway* (connection-pool exhaustion), *fraud-scoring* (slow model responses), and *wallet-service* (deposits credited late). *ledger-service* and withdrawals were not affected [\u200bS1\u200b].\n\n* **Withdrawal-processing stall (INC-2047, 18 Mar 2026)** - caused by\n  * **CHG-1047** - a migration that created index `idx_entries_account_created` on the *ledger_entries* table (started 22:00 UTC) [\u200bS4\u200b].\n  * Affected services were *ledger-service* (blocked writes), *wallet-service* (withdrawal requests timed out), and *payment-gateway* (payouts to PayFlex and CardNova not initiated) [\u200bS4\u200b].\n\nBoth incidents are confirmed by the final post-mortems (S1, S4) and summarised in the Q1 2026 reliability review (S3), which attributes the March deposit delay to CHG-1042 and CHG-1051 and the March withdrawal stall to CHG-1047 [\u200bS3\u200b].",
